---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { author } from "../../config/author";

const personSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Person",
  name: author.name,
  jobTitle: author.role,
  description:
    "Operations and compliance professional with experience at ACX (Australian Crypto Exchange) and Huobi Australia. Part of the team behind one of the first arbitrage crypto trading bots.",
  url: "/about/author",
  knowsAbout: [
    "cryptocurrency exchanges",
    "crypto compliance",
    "perpetual futures",
    "funding rates",
    "arbitrage trading",
  ],
  worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "FeeScope" },
};
---

<Layout title={`${author.name} — FeeScope`} description={`${author.name} — operational and compliance professional, founder of FeeScope.`}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(personSchema)} />

  <article class="mx-auto max-w-[700px] space-y-8 text-neutral-200">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-neutral-50">{author.name}</h1>
    <p class="text-neutral-400">{author.role}</p>

    <section class="space-y-4 text-neutral-300">
      <p>
        Sanjar Talaibekovic is an operations and compliance professional who has been
        working in crypto since the 2017 cycle. He was an operational and compliance
        manager at ACX (Australian Crypto Exchange) through the 2018 crypto winter,
        then moved into compliance at Huobi Australia as a Compliance Officer.
      </p>
      <p>
        At ACX, he was part of the team behind one of the first arbitrage crypto
        trading bots — an automated system that bought and sold across exchanges to
        capture price differences. That experience shaped everything since: he saw
        first-hand how much of crypto is noise, how hard it is to find the specific
        information that matters, and what happens when traders don't understand the
        rules of the market they're trading. People lost money they couldn't afford
        to lose.
      </p>
      <p>FeeScope is his answer to that problem.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-50">Why FeeScope exists</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-300">
        The first time you look at a funding rate, you think it's free money. It
        isn't. That's the thing almost no one explains when you're new — funding is a
        real cost that compounds, and it's different on every exchange. For an
        experienced trader, it's a line item. For a new one, it's invisible until
        it's already been paid.
      </p>
      <p class="text-neutral-300">
        FeeScope exists to make that cost visible before it's paid, in plain
        language, for both kinds of traders.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-50">What FeeScope is / isn't</h2>
      <p class="font-medium text-neutral-100">IS:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-6 text-neutral-300">
        <li>A data tool that shows current funding rates across venues, side by side, with the actual cost of holding</li>
        <li>Built on direct exchange APIs, refreshed every 8 hours, with per-venue rates cross-checked against the source</li>
        <li>Free</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="font-medium text-neutral-100">ISN'T:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-6 text-neutral-300">
        <li>Financial advice</li>
        <li>A signal service</li>
        <li>A recommendation engine</li>
        <li>A promise of returns</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-50">On AI use</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-300">
        Some code and copy on this site was developed with AI assistance. Every
        funding rate is pulled directly from public exchange APIs and cross-checked
        against the source. The methodology is documented in docs/FUNDING_PIPELINE.md.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-50">Affiliate disclosure</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-300">
        This site may include affiliate links to exchanges in the future. If you sign
        up through a link, we may earn a commission at no cost to you. This does not
        affect which venues are shown or how they're ranked.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-50">Contact</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-300">
        Corrections, questions, or feedback: <a href={`mailto:${author.contact}`} class="text-neutral-100 underline">{author.contact}</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
